On an annual basis at 25 forward P/E equities "correct sideways" at 4% annually assuming all future earnings are "known" So an unchanged so price for six months suggests equities have cheapened by 2%.

A change in discount rate of 75bp for equities "should" be worth roughly 8-10% on the price of equities.  

An unchanged equity price is partly correcting sideways by 2% and partly richening by 8%.  So net the sideways move over the last 6 months is stocks getting 6% richer assuming all future earnings were known

